  "query_preview": "..Recent satellite imagery shows mostly clear skies\nacross the region, with areas of valley fog quickly dissipating \nlate this morning across portions of the Wasatch Back, Cache \nValley, and Upper Sevier River Valleys. Building high pressure \nwill bring stable conditions and a warming, drying trend to the \nregion through at least Monday, with temperatures rising to 5 to\n10 degrees above normal. \n\nOn Tuesday, a dry shortwave trough will graze across northern \nUtah, producing a minimal drop in temperatures by a few degrees \nalongside 700-mb temperatures dropping to around 0C to +2C from \naround +5C on Monday. This shortwave could also act to mix out any\ndeveloping valley haze, though it's unclear whether or not the \nsubtle mixing will be enough to fully mix out valleys. \nAfterwards, high pressure will return with temperatures rising \nonce again through at least the end of the week.\n\nForecast confidence drops substantively after Friday. Ensemble\nguidance suggests a cooler, wetter trend heading into next\nweekend, though around 35% of ensemble members still favor higher\n500-mb heights and ridging next Saturday.",
